# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ToonAge for WoW Forever — the client reads THIS file, not _Mainline.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# THE FILENAME IS THE ONLY THING HERE THAT IS NOT OURS. DO NOT "FIX" IT.
#
# Everywhere else in this project the client is called Forever, because that is
# its name and ours is the vocabulary that should stick. The filename cannot
# be: WoW's addon loader picks a TOC by matching a fixed suffix it already
# knows, and the suffix it maps to this client is the one below. "Camelot" was
# Blizzard's internal codename for the project; it leaked before the game was
# announced as Forever and never got cleaned out of the loader.
#
# So a file named ToonAge_Forever.toc is a name the loader has never heard of.
# It is not read at all. That is not hypothetical -- it is what this project
# shipped, and the cost was that Forever fell through to ToonAge_Mainline.toc
# and loaded the ENTIRE retail product: 45 guide files, 433 KB of retail
# rotations, every retail module, on a Vanilla-era client that can use none of
# it. Nearly every "Forever inherited retail's problems" bug traces to here.
#
# Verified against a shipping addon on this same client rather than assumed:
# Questie ships Questie_Camelot.toc at ## Interface: 16001 beside a Questie.toc
# at 11508/11509, and the suffixed file is the only one listing its three
# Forever modules (ForeverCompat, ForeverObjectiveTracker, ForeverQuestData).
# Those modules work in game, so the loader is reading the suffix.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT
#
#   Data/Retail etc.   Only Data/Forever ships here, and only what the Forever
#                      client itself reported (see the harvest section below). Retail numbers
#                      are wrong for this content, and wrong numbers that look
#                      researched are worse than no numbers at all.
#
#                      Data/Forever/ApiManifest.lua is not game data at all:
#                      it is measured from THIS TOC's own files by
#                      Tools/gen_api_manifest.py, and it lists which client
#                      functions those files call. ApiGuard probes it at login
#                      and reports what this client does not have. That is the
#                      one thing about Forever nobody has written down, and
#                      every crash it has produced -- GetSpecialization,
#                      GetLootSlotLink, GetItemInfoInstant -- was this list
#                      being discovered one error at a time instead.
#   Core/StatEngine    Retail diminishing-returns math. Meaningless here.
#   The guide stack    Forever ships no guides. QuestTracker, Arrow, MapPins,
#                      AntTrail, CoordResolver and the Guide* modules all point
#                      at guide steps that do not exist.
#   Every advisor      Gear, Rotation, Talents, Professions, Pets, Delves,
#                      Weekly: all of them rank things using Data/Retail.
#
# ToonAge_Mainline.toc still carries 16001 as a fallback. If this file is ever
# not read, the addon still loads there, and Core/Profile.lua's allow-list is
# the second gate that keeps the retail modules from initializing.

# ── Libraries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Libs\LibStub.lua
Libs\WagoAnalytics\Shim.lua

# ── Core engine (flavour-neutral) ─────────────────────────────────────
Core\Init.lua
Core\Environment.lua
Core\Compat\API.lua
Core\Utils.lua
Core\State.lua
Core\UI.lua
Core\UIModern.lua
Core\Layout.lua
# Reads tooltip lines GetItemStats cannot see (Equip:/Use:/proc text).
# Shared with the TBC build; the gear tab shows those lines per item.
Core\TooltipScan.lua
Core\MinimapButton.lua
Core\ApiGuard.lua
Core\Profile.lua
Core\Analytics.lua

# ── Sourced reference (names and roles only, each spec cites its guide) ──
# Icy Veins WoW Forever spec guides, read 2026-09-27. Not game numbers.
Data\Forever\Coach.lua

# ── Measured game data (generated from the Forever harvest) ──────────
# Tools/gen_forever_data.lua turns the harvest in the saved file into these.
# Every value is what this client reported -- tooltips verbatim, trained
# levels, stat blocks -- so every player gets what one account measured.
Data\Forever\Racials.lua
Data\Forever\Spells.lua
Data\Forever\Talents.lua
Data\Forever\Items.lua
Data\Forever\SpellRanks.lua

# ── Measured API surface ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not game data: generated from the file list below. See the note above.
Data\Forever\ApiManifest.lua

# ── Infrastructure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modules\Infrastructure\ErrorLog.lua
Modules\Infrastructure\Settings.lua
Modules\Infrastructure\ChatCopy.lua
Modules\Infrastructure\CoordHarvester.lua

# ── Quality of life ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each reads the world through APIs this client has and carries no expansion
# numbers of its own. Cross-module calls all go through TA:GetModule, which
# returns nil for anything absent, and every call site nil-guards -- verified,
# not assumed, before this list was trimmed.
Modules\Progression\XPTracker.lua
Modules\Automation\RestOptimizer.lua
Modules\Automation\DeathRecovery.lua

# ── Farming ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GatherTracker records node positions on LOOT_OPENED. Its dot renderer drew
# on the HUD, which this build no longer ships -- that render path is
# nil-guarded and now does nothing, so the module is record-only until it has
# a tab of its own.
Modules\Farming\GatherTracker.lua

# ── Measured play ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
